            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "IDK, I think it is expected if the user straight up **deletes** the lua stdlib, then nvim is going to crash. c.f. `_G.vim = nil`. rewriting every single `lua_getfield` in the codebase because of an artificial crash (the o.g. example in the bug report did in fact not illustrate the problem the user had) is going to be a wild goose chase for little benefit. \n\nIMO just checking that `traceback` is a function is enough (and would have caught the users original error of just `debug.traceback` being missing, not all of `debug`).\n",
            "commit_id": "b5c6f817096fea6be2344bb2e6bd669e66ce8f21",
            "created_at": "2026-08-26T18:00:48Z",
